Replicas of the Imperial regalia of Japan including Yata no Kagami are included in {{ill|Masakaki|8=en|simple|user:Immanuelle/Masakaki|12=draft|12=draft}} at Shinto shrines.<ref name="d-2015a2">{{Cite web |last=D |first=John |date=2015-04-05 |title=The Colours of Shinto (masakaki) |url=https://www.greenshinto.com/2015/04/05/the-colours-of-shinto/ |access-date=2023-11-27 |website=Green Shinto |language=en-GB}}</ref> Masakaki come in sets of two, with the left one containing a replica of {{ill|Kusanagi no Tsurugi|8=en|simple|user:Immanuelle/Kusanagi no Tsurugi|12=draft|12=draft}} and the right one containing a replica of Yata no Kagami and {{ill|Yasakani-no-Magatama|8=en|simple|user:Immanuelle/Yasakani-no-Magatama|12=draft|12=draft}}.<ref name="d-2015a2" /> {{ill|Mirrors in Shinto|8=en|simple|User:Immanuelle/Shinto mirror|12=draft|12=draft}} are highly significant with Yata no Kagami being seen as prototypical to them.<ref name="degaris-2013a">{{Cite book |last=De_Garis |first=Frederick |url=https://books.google.com/books?id=hUm0AAAAQBAJ&pg=PA237 |title=We Japanese |date=2013-09-05 |publisher=Routledge |isbn=978-1-136-18367-6 |pages=237 |language=en}}</ref><ref name="D-2012a" />

